# Renovate (renovate.json) bumps every tool below except checkov in one grouped
# "toolchain" PR, together with each in-repo copy of the version (workflows,
# envs/tfc-admin, scripts/setup.sh, .terraform-version). Two copies need a
# reviewer: refresh OPA_SHA256 and SC_SHA256 in terraform-plan.yml with
# scripts/tool-checksums.sh, and confirm HCP Terraform offers the new OPA.
#
# AWS provider (hashicorp/aws) is NOT managed here. It is pinned per-module in
# each module's/root's versions.tf (>= 6.46.0, < 7.0.0), not via asdf.
# AWS roots/modules (modules/aws/**, envs/aws/**) auto-flow through
# validate-all / lint / test / docs / security because scripts/terraform-roots.sh
# discovers roots structurally and has no cloud filter.
# CI validates roots in a fixed number of shards (terraform-plan.yml), so the
# root count no longer approaches GitHub's 256-leg matrix cap. CI needs
# registry egress to download the hashicorp/aws provider.
#
# trivy replaces tfsec (EOL, folded into Trivy): kept equal to the
# trivy-action `version:` in .github/workflows/reusable-security.yml.
# checkov: CI runs the image that bridgecrewio/checkov-action pins (a Dependabot
# update), so Renovate skips it; set this to that image tag when the action moves.
# check-jsonschema (pip/pipx, not asdf): `make config-check`; the meta-lint pip
# pin and the pre-commit rev move in the Renovate toolchain PR.
# opa: equal to OPA_VERSION in the opa job of terraform-plan.yml (`make opa-test`).
# shellcheck: the pre-commit hook pins shellcheck-py v<this>.1.
terraform 1.17.1
tflint 0.62.0
trivy 0.70.0
shellcheck 0.11.0
terraform-docs 0.19.0
checkov 3.3.17
opa 1.22.2
